# Shell scripts end up executed inside Linux containers - the cypress test image COPYs them
# straight in - where a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named `bash\r` and
# then report the script itself as "required file not found", which points at the wrong file
# entirely. Keep them LF in the working tree whatever core.autocrlf is set to locally.
*.sh text eol=lf
